This chapter specifies how the compiler turns Morloc source into the
artifacts described in <<build-architecture>>. It begins with a map of the
pipeline. It then follows a program through it: parsing and module
loading, typechecking, effects, term sharing, realization, segmentation into
pools, serialization, ownership and code generation. It ends with how the
manifest's command interface is derived, how a new language is brought into
Morloc, and the API of the runtime library, which is the contract every
language binding is written against.

